/T (    For Version 1, I focused on the mechanical design, structural optimization, and simulation of my 6-DOF robotic arm. Using SOLIDWORKS and ANSYS, I designed and optimized the mechanical components to improve their strength-to-weight ratio while maintaining important mounting features. I also tested several components' tolerances and revised the design to improve fit and overall assembly.)
/E (    For Version 1, I focused on the mechanical design, structural optimization, and simulation of my 6-DOF robotic arm. Using SOLIDWORKS and ANSYS, I designed and optimized the mechanical components to improve their strength-to-weight ratio while maintaining important mounting features. I also tested several components' tolerances and revised the design to improve fit and overall assembly.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 94 0 R
/T (For the kinematic analysis, I developed a mathematical model of the entire 6-DOF robotic arm and calculated the Jacobian matrix to better understand the relationship between joint velocities and end-effector motion. I then used MATLAB's Robotics System Toolbox to simulate joint movements for J1 through J4. By implementing smooth motion interpolation, I simulated different joint configurations and visualized how the robotic arm moves.)
/E (For the kinematic analysis, I developed a mathematical model of the entire 6-DOF robotic arm and calculated the Jacobian matrix to better understand the relationship between joint velocities and end-effector motion. I then used MATLAB's Robotics System Toolbox to simulate joint movements for J1 through J4. By implementing smooth motion interpolation, I simulated different joint configurations and visualized how the robotic arm moves.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
