1341 0 obj
<<
/Title (The load cell measures weight with strain gauges. When a weight is placed on the platform, it bends, and the strain gauges measure the resulting compression and tension. With all five weights loaded, the load cell read -4.9183 kg. Its last unloading reading was 0.0032 kg, close to zero but not exactly zero. The same least squares method gave y = 0.4963 - 0.9841x for the averaged data, with a correlation coefficient of -0.999999 and a standard error of 0.0029 kg. The line is essentially perfectly linear, and its slope is close to 1 in magnitude.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 904 0 R
/Prev 1220 0 R
/Next 1221 0 R
>>
